{title: Cúmplase, Oh Cristo, Tu Voluntad}
{artist: Adelaide Pollard}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 72}

Verse 1
[Eb]Cúmplase, oh [Ab]Cristo, tu voluntad.
[Bb]Sólo [Eb]tú puedes [Ab]mi alma [Bb]salvar.
[Eb]Cual [Ab]alfarero, [Eb]para [Cm]tu [Eb]honor
Vasija útil [Ab]hazme, [Eb]Señor.

Verse 2
[Eb]Cúmplase, oh [Ab]Cristo, [Eb]tu voluntad
Quita [Bb]de mi [Ab]alma [F]toda maldad.
[Bb]Cual [Eb]blanca nieve [Ab]hazla [Cm]fulgir,
[Eb]Y fiel y [Ab]humilde [Bb]hazme [Eb]vivir.

Verse 3
[Eb]Cúmplase, oh [Ab]Cristo, tu [Bb]voluntad.
[Eb]Toda [Ab]dolencia [F]puedes [Bb]sanar;
[Eb]Cuitas, pesares, [Ab]con [Cm]tu [Eb]poder
Quieres [Ab]hacerlos [Eb]desvanecer

Verse 4
[Eb]Cúmplase, oh [Ab]Cristo, [Eb]tu voluntad.
Mora [Bb]en [Eb]mi alma, [Ab]dale [F]tu paz,
[Bb]Para [Eb]que el mundo [Ab]vea [Cm]tu amor,
[Eb]Tu obra perfecta, [Ab]oh [Bb]buen [Eb]Salvador.
